        "raw": "<p>Hello,</p><p>With the very last set of Sentinels of the Multiverse being Kickstarted right now- the story of the Multiverse will be coming to an end. I figured a fun and low key way to celebrate the end of an awesome game would be to campaign the whole thing. I spent the last week compiling a list of everything in the game- so we can campaign the whole story chronologically.</p><p>I looked through a few other groups campaign and decided to keep it somewhat simple as far as general rules.&nbsp; I noticed alot of them had away rules and return villain strikes- but I decided to bypass those and use Unlocked Variants as return villain strikes instead.&nbsp; We are going to use the concept that first game is on normal difficulty- if the group wins the next villain begins on advanced difficulty.&nbsp; If the fight is lost than the next battle is reset to normal- including a direct re-match.</p><p><span class=\"text_exposed_show\">We will have to defeat all of the (core) villains in a set to unlock the next set, variant characters, and environments. <u>Every</u> currently unlocked villain must be defeated to unlock the next set.&nbsp; We will try to capture all of the villains right up and into the release of the final set. Every defeated villain is captured and cannot come back unless it has a variant form left. When a villain is selected- their hero nemesis is automatically drafted into the battle. If we lose the battle that hero is lost and cannot return unless in variant form. <span class=\"text_exposed_show\">If there is no nemesis available- open select the heroes for the game- just know if the group loses a dice roll determines the captured hero.&nbsp; </span>Defeat all of the villains and win, lose all of the heroes and it&#39;s game over!</span></p><p>I am attaching the list I compiled - the list is an attempt to approach things chronologically overall- but that is easier said than done. I integrated The Cauldron and some of the Yoshi material into the list as well so I just chose points in where those characters would be introduced into the Multiverse.&nbsp; If you choose to use the list- just know it is not fully finished pending future information that may come out in OblivAeon and in The Cauldron Storm Fall- so you will have to update those yourself.</p><p>I just wanted to put this out there if anybody wanted to put it to use / continue it on their own.&nbsp; I appreciate any input but please know that I will not be updating it further on here.&nbsp; Enjoy!</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
